  "id": "COMPOUND:27495 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (Z)-Pentadecenoic acid may interact with prostate cells, through its interaction with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This enzyme is a target of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, which in turn targets prostate cells. Additionally, (Z)-Pentadecenoic acid is linked to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, and this enzyme is also a target of Npc15336, which further targets prostate cells. The evidence supports a pathway where (Z)-Pentadecenoic acid may modulate the activity of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, potentially influencing the signaling pathways that regulate prostate cell function. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple targets in the pathway, suggesting a possible role in cellular regulation. The evidence is consistent with a direct interaction between (Z)-Pentadecenoic acid and prostate cells, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
